  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Earthquake in T&#xfc;rkiye and Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project, IOM proposes to provide humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable earthquake-affected populations inside northwest Syria (NWS) and support these crisis-affected groups with emergency NFI services. Through these activities, IOM plans to support 14,225 earthquake-affected individuals, including internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host community members. 
 
Under Outcome 1 (NFI), IOM will contribute to lifesaving and life-sustaining winterization activities by improving displaced populations&#x2019; access to full NFI kits by pre-positioning 2,000 full NFI kits and 845 shelter repair kits (estimated one kit per family). IOM will work through pre-approved Rapid Response Mechanism (RRM) partners to distribute the kits to most vulnerable households.</narrative>
  </description>
